{:edb/db-before-t 2269 :edb/db-after-t 2270 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535582 50 #inst "2026-10-09T02:56:47.568Z" 13194139535582 true] [17592186129133 1020 #edb/ref 17592186356020 13194139535582 true] [17592186129135 1020 #edb/ref 17592186356006 13194139535582 true] [17592186129135 1020 #edb/ref 17592186356034 13194139535582 true] [17592186129210 1020 #edb/ref 17592186356013 13194139535582 true] [17592186129210 1020 #edb/ref 17592186356027 13194139535582 true] [17592186356006 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356007 13194139535582 true] [17592186356006 1089 "q-161052" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356006 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535582 true] [17592186356006 1100 "Integrate the function $f(x,y)=4{y}^{2}$ over the disk of radius $3$ centered at the origin." 13194139535582 true] [17592186356006 1113 #uuid "2686fcc3-f583-5dd7-b59b-47c6ab685620" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356006 1145 "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/0a1de805051eff4ea82b4eefb7bb113c724b3d4e7304704831b6294ee4e4d674.png)\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 3,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}4{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}4(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{3}4{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{[{r}^{4}]}_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta (81-0)\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =81{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =81{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}{[\\theta -\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}[(2\\pi -0)-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =81\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356008 13194139535582 true] [17592186356007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356009 13194139535582 true] [17592186356007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356010 13194139535582 true] [17592186356007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356011 13194139535582 true] [17592186356007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356012 13194139535582 true] [17592186356007 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535582 true] [17592186356007 1041 "selection" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356007 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356011 13194139535582 true] [17592186356007 1110 #uuid "67b6c25a-4750-56e9-a4a0-95464fd6b14d" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356008 1034 "9\\pi " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356008 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356008 1111 #uuid "87171f87-1c34-5563-95f5-41dcd6eba908" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356009 1034 "18+2\\pi " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356009 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356009 1111 #uuid "e62f01e1-fa78-5188-a518-dcd46fb2382b" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356010 1034 "9+4\\pi " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356010 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356010 1111 #uuid "b8b3a64b-2cc9-5891-8a47-13b2fd86ad91" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356011 1034 "81\\pi " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356011 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356011 1111 #uuid "ebf2ff55-b81f-5358-8ef0-6929c218400f" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356012 1034 "27\\pi " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356012 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356012 1111 #uuid "e55f6f64-7e78-5a6e-a7bf-6d4d57d69a13" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356013 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356014 13194139535582 true] [17592186356013 1089 "q-161065" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356013 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535582 true] [17592186356013 1100 "If $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 1},$ then ${∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A=$" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356013 1113 #uuid "a7b778e2-1e49-5fc9-b2a9-e6236a05633d" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356013 1145 "We need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA={∬}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/f0417011f46d3860b7de86fe652a7d80dd9787cb05c2057601b41c17e0c2b423.png)\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents the disk of radius $1$ centered at $(0,1).$\n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the ${x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =1 \\\\ {(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1)}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1 & =1 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire circle, we must have $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits for $r$ and $\\theta .$ First of all, $r$ can vary from $r=0$ (at the origin) to $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ (at the boundary of the region): \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/3f4bb1428a6cc9b7e191e1904636d654145d9a1f2fb1dd40843d8cd878194772.png)\n\nSecondly, $\\theta $ can vary between $\\theta =0$ (the positive $x$-axis) and $\\theta =\\pi $ (the negative $x$-axis):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/d6f4e054767650cd2a3d348aee8210af421e2df21792d79f42c5a58b5f4e82e6.png)\n\nSo, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356015 13194139535582 true] [17592186356014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356016 13194139535582 true] [17592186356014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356017 13194139535582 true] [17592186356014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356018 13194139535582 true] [17592186356014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356019 13194139535582 true] [17592186356014 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535582 true] [17592186356014 1041 "selection" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356014 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356015 13194139535582 true] [17592186356014 1110 #uuid "dcc08679-7f6a-5262-8a25-a6b96bf12b00" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356015 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356015 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356015 1111 #uuid "d954d846-c533-551a-a82f-65f751f2e734" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356016 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356016 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356016 1111 #uuid "7ba221ec-f275-5c06-8a6c-cf7341a30dda" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356017 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356017 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356017 1111 #uuid "e8b14a46-949b-50e7-93d9-24aef2229e35" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356018 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356018 1111 #uuid "fa9b2736-8f14-51d7-9790-3ce6a610b82e" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356019 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356019 1111 #uuid "305f601d-a355-5355-8e31-2a43aa1a2b71" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356020 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356021 13194139535582 true] [17592186356020 1089 "q-38133" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356020 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535582 true] [17592186356020 1100 "${\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356020 1113 #uuid "bd8c290c-46b0-546e-b105-a7371cbafeab" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356020 1145 "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}}{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}2{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}2{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={[\\theta +\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356022 13194139535582 true] [17592186356021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356023 13194139535582 true] [17592186356021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356024 13194139535582 true] [17592186356021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356025 13194139535582 true] [17592186356021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356026 13194139535582 true] [17592186356021 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535582 true] [17592186356021 1041 "selection" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356021 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356023 13194139535582 true] [17592186356021 1110 #uuid "0d84eefc-a3a7-5e23-a25b-2fec9b265db9" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356022 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356022 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356022 1111 #uuid "e14a0e64-5cb8-5161-9283-7cdbc438df70" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356023 1034 "\\pi " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356023 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356023 1111 #uuid "2eaad03e-529a-52c6-909e-f109880976f0" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356024 1034 "\\pi +4" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356024 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356024 1111 #uuid "5c657196-04d0-5b2a-800d-a9c23cfdede3" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356025 1034 "2\\pi " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356025 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356025 1111 #uuid "f7313f7a-b58a-581d-8b88-6ace41c36b14" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356026 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356026 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356026 1111 #uuid "0a97a54a-fa79-53e7-838b-ca93fc0cf2f9" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356027 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356028 13194139535582 true] [17592186356027 1089 "q-83955" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356027 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535582 true] [17592186356027 1100 "If $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\le \\frac{1}{4},\\,x\\le 0},$ then ${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A=$" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356027 1113 #uuid "1b9a1961-cfec-5ea0-aa17-358f76216410" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356027 1145 "We need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/32c4bf490df51121ddf1575df8211033185d392fd5b08519971723b820da191f.png)\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $\\frac{1}{2}$ centered at $(0,\\frac{1}{2}).$ \n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the ${x}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits for $r$ and $\\theta .$ First of all, $r$ can vary from $r=0$ (at the origin) to $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ (at the boundary of the region): \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/b1e2eac0041d0b0cb802561b3fb83fd8fab1b940cb6c42f698879837c06cbff0.png)\n\nSecondly, $\\theta $ can vary between $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (the positive $y$-axis) and $\\theta =\\pi $ (the negative $x$-axis):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/193601785ff94605d12b91b7cab1e7390af532ba1912530bd8d3f492324e2788.png)\n\nSo, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2})\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356028 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356029 13194139535582 true] [17592186356028 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356030 13194139535582 true] [17592186356028 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356031 13194139535582 true] [17592186356028 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356032 13194139535582 true] [17592186356028 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356033 13194139535582 true] [17592186356028 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535582 true] [17592186356028 1041 "selection" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356028 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356029 13194139535582 true] [17592186356028 1110 #uuid "07a72c4f-3304-568e-a551-c9fb31d124be" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356029 1034 "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356029 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356029 1111 #uuid "a79d912a-f0a9-54d0-a0b2-43fc4aca87b2" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356030 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356030 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356030 1111 #uuid "6f68930e-0b47-5542-af81-e3a94b899b5d" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356031 1034 "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356031 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356031 1111 #uuid "cff20bea-7439-522f-bd59-fcd12d27d5d6" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356032 1034 "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356032 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356032 1111 #uuid "e98fa51f-6a62-5c8d-84df-226873f293c3" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356033 1034 "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139535582 true] [17592186356033 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356033 1111 #uuid "a4e9eba4-c286-5817-972f-9758ee803cb0" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356034 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356035 13194139535582 true] [17592186356034 1089 "q-83970" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356034 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535582 true] [17592186356034 1100 "Integrate the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}$ over the portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at the origin, where $x\\le 0$ and $y\\le 0.$" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356034 1113 #uuid "0d3937fa-c397-5c82-8e5c-164ecad0379b" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356034 1145 "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/e4275e74a45deb22c0ed22546772e33fbd5caeb89a4036b1a2f4870e8ecf67a1.png)\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 1,\\,\\pi \\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{2}{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+1}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2r}{{r}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}+1)]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2[\\theta ]_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi \\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356035 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356036 13194139535582 true] [17592186356035 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356037 13194139535582 true] [17592186356035 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356038 13194139535582 true] [17592186356035 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356039 13194139535582 true] [17592186356035 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356040 13194139535582 true] [17592186356035 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535582 true] [17592186356035 1041 "selection" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356035 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356036 13194139535582 true] [17592186356035 1110 #uuid "e673c351-c42f-5bfc-ade1-34e17eb7be97" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356036 1034 "\\frac{\\pi \\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356036 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356036 1111 #uuid "609a2895-a79e-516a-9893-127b9904b94f" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356037 1034 "\\pi \\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356037 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356037 1111 #uuid "bbd33aed-f9c6-5292-b4ef-01f954584970" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356038 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356038 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356038 1111 #uuid "08fdce84-3d28-5b2d-a3b7-6a87f663b77a" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356039 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356039 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356039 1111 #uuid "a4317ef3-816f-5a45-a27f-0d7ae893de3e" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356040 1034 "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}" 13194139535582 true] [17592186356040 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535582 true] [17592186356040 1111 #uuid "68d17e28-6492-5229-aaee-4302b188b3e6" 13194139535582 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-161052" 17592186356006 "q-161052/selection" 17592